### What are common mistakes?

```java
// WRONG: workers are NOT idempotent
// Crash → re-delivery → double-charge customer!

// CORRECT: dedup by job ID
if (processedJobs.existsById(jobId)) return; // already done
processedJobs.save(jobId);
```

### What should a senior engineer know?

- The whole design assumes idempotent workers because of at-least-once delivery.
- Monitor queue depth, job age, retry counts, and DLQ volume.
- For ordered jobs within an entity, route them to the same shard by entity ID.
- Long-running jobs must extend the lease (heartbeat) to avoid re-delivery while still running.
